# System UI Overlay Styling Rule

## Overview
All screens must ensure that the system status bar (top) and system navigation bar (bottom) visually integrate with the app's design by matching the closest color.

## Rules

### Status Bar (Top)
- **Default**: Match the background color of the main scaffold/content area
- **If content has multiple colors**: Match the color of the topmost/header section
- **Icon brightness**: Light icons for dark backgrounds, dark icons for light backgrounds

### Navigation Bar (Bottom)
- **Default**: Match the background color of the main scaffold/content area  
- **If content has multiple colors**: Match the color of the bottommost/navigation section
- **Icon brightness**: Light icons for dark backgrounds, dark icons for light backgrounds

## Implementation Pattern

Use `AnnotatedRegion<SystemUiOverlayStyle>` wrapping the Scaffold:

```dart
AnnotatedRegion<SystemUiOverlayStyle>(
  value: SystemUiOverlayStyle(
    statusBarColor: Colors.black,           // Match top area
    statusBarIconBrightness: Brightness.light,
    systemNavigationBarColor: Colors.black, // Match bottom area
    systemNavigationBarIconBrightness: Brightness.light,
  ),
  child: Scaffold(
    backgroundColor: Colors.black,
    // ... rest of screen
  ),
)
```

## Screen-Specific Guidelines

### Auth Screens (Login, Signup, OTP, Role Selection)
- **Signup & OTP** (match [LoadingScreen]): Scaffold + bottom nav **`MerchantColors.bgMain`** (`#0E2A44`); status bar **`MerchantColors.bgHeader`** (`#0B1F33`) — same as splash/loading.
- **Login** and other auth surfaces may still use the older dark navy (`#0F1A29`) until aligned; prefer matching loading when refreshing auth UI.

### Storefront & Merchant Pages
- Status bar + Navigation bar: **Cream** (`StorefrontColors.cream`)
- This matches the storefront background

### Client Pages
- Status bar + Navigation bar: **White** (`Colors.white`)
- This matches light backgrounds

### Screens with Bottom Navigation Bar
- Status bar: Match header/content background
- Navigation bar: Match bottom navigation bar background (usually **Navy** `StorefrontColors.navyDark`)

## When Colors Don't Match
If a screen has layered colors:
1. Status bar → Match the **header/top section** color
2. Navigation bar → Match the **bottom navigation or footer** color

## Example: Login Screen
```
┌─ Status bar: Dark Navy (matches scaffold bg)
├─ Header section: Dark Navy
├─ Form section: Dark Navy
└─ Navigation bar: Dark Navy (matches scaffold bg)
```

## Example: Merchant Storefront
```
┌─ Status bar: Cream (matches header)
├─ Header with banner: Cream background
├─ Content: Cream background
├─ Bottom nav: Navy
└─ Navigation bar: Navy (matches bottom nav)
```

## Testing Checklist
- [ ] Status bar color visible on all screens
- [ ] Navigation bar color visible on all screens
- [ ] Icons are readable (proper brightness)
- [ ] Colors match adjacent screen content
- [ ] No jarring color transitions
- [ ] Works on both light and dark backgrounds
